--TEST--
Core\Str::upperFirst/lowerFirst are Unicode-aware where ucfirst/lcfirst are byte-wise
--ORACLE-DIVERGES--
ADR 0009: `string` is guaranteed-valid UTF-8, so the first *character* is case-mapped; `ucfirst` maps the first *byte* and leaves any multi-byte one alone.
--FILE--
<?mwl
echo Core\Str::upperFirst("mwl rocks"), "\n";
echo Core\Str::lowerFirst("MWL"), "\n";
echo Core\Str::upperFirst("élan"), "\n";
echo Core\Str::lowerFirst("Élan"), "\n";
--EXPECT--
Mwl rocks
mWL
Élan
élan
